WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Venezuela’s dictator dances

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.360
right outside, people suffer and die.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.920
It's so cruel and unnecessary.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.280
Venezuela&nbsp;should be rich.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.280
Not long ago

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.520
Venezuela was the richest country in Latin America.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.760
It still has greater oil reserves than Saudi Arabia.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.120
But today

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.780
Venezuelans starve.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.160
These people are fighting over bags of flour.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.640
Then there’s the violence.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.120
One Venezuelan is murdered every 20 mins.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.120
So are American celebrities who

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.620
praised Hugo Chávez' "people's revolution”&nbsp;now

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.480
embarrassed by what they said?

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.440
Will they admit they were wrong?

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.140
Leftist intellectual Noam Chomsky&nbsp;fawned over Chávez

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.200
said he’s created a better world.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.880
I can see how a better world is being created,

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.300
and can speak to the person who’s inspired it.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.240
Actor Sean Penn met with Chávez and said this:

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.600
He’s done at the moment,

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.140
incredible things for the 80% of the people that are

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.360
very poor there.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.840
Actor Danny Glover did some playful boxing

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.360
and hugging with Chávez.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.800
Then he praised his "vision for humanity."

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.060
Michael Moore claimed Chávez eliminated

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.740
"75% of extreme poverty.”

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:22.860
C’mon Michael,

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.140
Chávez&nbsp;added&nbsp;to extreme poverty.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.880
Who is Hugo Chávez?

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.680
Director Oliver Stone made this insipid film

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:31.760
celebrating Chávez and Latin American socialism.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.520
Take an incredible look

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.240
at an extraordinary movement.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.000
No, they’re not.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.160
Now they starve and fear&nbsp;they’ll be killed.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.360
Model Naomi Campbell went to&nbsp;Venezuela&nbsp;and said,

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.980
“I’m amazed to see the love for social programs."

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.960
We asked all of them if they’d talk about

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.720
their love of Chávez

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.100
Only one responded.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.560
Noam Chomsky.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.140
His&nbsp;anti-capitalist teachings have misled

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.700
millions of students.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.960
But they’ve worked for Chomsky

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.000
After he praised Chávez's "sharp poverty reduction”

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.720
Chávez returned the favor by

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.440
holding up Chomsky's book at the UN.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.260
That made it a best-seller.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.080
So is Chomsky now ashamed of his praise?

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.480
"No," he wrote me.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.800
He said at the time he praised Chávez,

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.900
"Venezuela&nbsp;had seen a remarkable

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:25.960
reduction in poverty."

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.680
He cited this Harvard magazine article.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.780
But this was written by&nbsp;a leftist who helped

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.220
write Oliver Stone’s movie.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:34.580
So I asked Chomsky,

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.080
given the current crisis in Venezuela

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.280
should you now say to the students who've

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.720
learned from you,

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.640
'socialism wrecks people's lives'?

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.240
Chomsky wrote back:

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.080
"I never described Chávez's state capitalist

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.100
government as 'socialist'

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.100
'Private capitalism remained'

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.320
'Capitalists were free to undermine

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.540
the economy in all sorts of ways, like

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:59.240
massive export of capital."

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.420
What?

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.580
Capitalists&nbsp;“exported capital and

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.340
"undermined the economy" by

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.120
abandoning their homes and

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.780
fleeing&nbsp;across&nbsp;the border to Columbia?

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:11.540
Thousands of Venezuelans cross daily in search of

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.560
of food, medicine, and work.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.180
These people are socialist fools.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:19.240
Useful idiots, Lenin would have called them.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.820
As much as I'd enjoy rubbing their noses in their

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.900
stupidity now, I cannot rejoice, because

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.360
know that&nbsp;Venezuela's descent into chaos

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.060
will not be the last time we hear of a dying

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.940
socialist economy.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.840
Socialism failed in all these places.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.900
We are yet to see one socialist country succeed.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.400
And yet sadly, they and other countries refuse

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.720
to learn from history

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.020
Other countries will give socialism a go.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:50.720
'Useful idiots,' will sing socialism's praises

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.720
until the last light goes out.

